405: \nL406: Dear Pashnite, the cite95†1999-era California Motorcycle Roads†web.archive.org you have used for the last 20 years to plan your rides still exists on the Internet Archive, but that site has been retired.\nL407: \nL408: <cite95†Click link to view Archive copy from 2005.†web.archive.org >\nL409: Over two decades later, it's time to rebuild. A lot of work will go into building a site like this from scratch. It will take time. Thousands of hours, years actually. I think only a crazy person would attempt a project like this. Which is why there is no equal. The cite95†original CMR†web.archive.org had 300 webpages of roads, 600 pages of text, thousands of photos, tens of thousands of links and was made up of 241,148 files. I would like to double that. It will take time to rebuild this site.\nL410: I appreciate your support over the last 20+ years. Hundreds more road pages are coming.  -Tim\nL411: Want to help? Pashnit is simply a hobby and labor of love. Consider donating $20 to help support this site. The all-new Pashnit.com California Motorcycle Roads site is 100% free to access by all. There are no ads, no gunk, no clutter, no popups because users support the growth of this site. Want to be the first to see new roads & articles that are steadily added?  Use subscribe link above.\nL412: cite13†Learn More about the Author... L413: \nL414: See more at cite15†www.PashnitTours.com†www.pashnittours.com L415: Watch short documentary about the author of Pashnit.com\nL416: #### Pashnit Road Map:\nL417: \nL418: cite23†Alderpoint Rd - Garberville\nL419: cite87†Ancient Bristlecone Pine Forest L420: \nL421: cite24†Avenue of the Giants L422: cite25†Bald Hills Rd - Orick to Hoopa\nL423: cite86†Bayne Rd - Coloma to Kelsey\nL424: \nL425: cite26†Benton Crossing Rd - Benton\nL426: \nL427: cite27†Berryessa Knoxville Rd - Lake Berryessa\nL428: cite29†Bolinas Ridge - Ridgecrest Blvd\nL429: cite28†Bodie Ghost Town L430: cite31†Branscomb